    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2HGywC1okeJg2iDuYSe2SYV)_\n\n**Before:** TODO headings in the docs of the configuration itself were invisible to the agenda, or mixed into the PARA views.\n\n**After:** `C-c o a c` lists every open TODO heading in the config's Org files, each line led by the file's `#+title:` instead of the Area/Project category.\n\n## Changes (`sp-agenda-views`, `sp-org-agenda` doc, CHANGELOG)\n- New view `c` built like the issue views (`sp-org-issues`): restricts `org-agenda-files` and binds `vulpea-para-agenda-inhibit-files-update`. Its `todo \"\"` block names no keyword: it matches any keyword that is not a done state, as `org-todo-keywords` or a file's `#+todo:` line define them.\n- Only this view changes `org-agenda-prefix-format`; `sp-agenda-views-file-title` reads the title from the buffer (file name as fallback).\n- **Source of files (my choice):** `sp-agenda-views-config-source` is `yadm` by default (`git ls-files '*.org'` on `sp-yadm-repo` with `~` as work tree); `dirs` searches `sp-agenda-views-config-dirs` instead. Empty result signals a `user-error`.\n- `sp-org-agenda` doc: new \"Config file views\" section with the setup and why file-set views, TODO keywords vs tags and file titles matter; key table updated.\n- CHANGELOG entry in \"Agenda, capture and task keywords\".\n\n## Tested\nEmacs 29.3 in batch with stubs for vulpea-para: both file sources return the right files (an untracked `.org` is skipped in yadm mode), and the agenda shows the file title or the file name. Default TODO keywords only; not run in the full config.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiByGEMc2iZouwYY3kJ",
